{"title":"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be two positive integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddf57a1507686a49e3d290b3542ccac565cd35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> different numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5c95d2b1ee6b025d757ee65818daba20a1abe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2,\\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> such that for any two indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec5455ff7287eff220419970f446c62a141943a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i \\leq j \\leq m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e5e672a139e0b30661cf241c72ce8d487c58ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_j \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, there exists an index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db842618336b3fe437d3cbda6739ed306832966b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_j = a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06990cbc064a33c31fe51653a1709b74d91f07c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1+a_2+...+a_m}{m} \\ge \\frac{n+1}{2}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6ad4d1f08a7101a9f3a3f405f14dd1d04053f83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy the given conditions. We will prove that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836dbc04fa187a752d17d3072d8d5bc24286c8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j, 1 \\le j \\le m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c8fe8c302849e44924782869e836fd7f211f7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_j+a_{m-j+1} \\ge n+1\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0364eecefa9628aeea94ebdfa9595f48e7f79534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; \\dots &lt; a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"12\" />. Assume that for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836dbc04fa187a752d17d3072d8d5bc24286c8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j, 1 \\le j \\le m,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a222a1ce664e746997f55eee95a8006f1709a4ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_j + a_{m-j+1} \\le n\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>This implies, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f41f23ad4b230060bdc694b36339bdbc9ae2e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, 1 \\le i \\le j,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba2a1e29da4588ab6fdb0a826ee9e203d368962.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i + a_{m-j+1} \\le n\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />\nbecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1678a7815d142666d97c7a4618d948484b1f7ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\le a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For each of these values of i, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f826f70099ca6c27f91661b250e2e8f36a971c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_{m-j+1} = a_{k_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c716c4550e367859e3771c3fac522daae19e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" /> is a member of the sequence for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d821cd7865ccc9d72d1293d18d881afd85362fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &gt; 0, a_{k_i} &gt; a_{m-j+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" />.\nCombining all of our conditions we have that each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0ac59ec3562b84367674cfe6245f223b892913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> must be distinct integers such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd2931d70cdc0e0776daa3386c8ae550409b63e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m-j+1 &lt; k_i \\le m\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>However, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0ac59ec3562b84367674cfe6245f223b892913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, but only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/1233d0dcd103cc6ee1353e914244e3d66573a39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> integers satisfying the above inequality, so we have a contradiction. Our assumption that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b66afd651880870169601b0781d49196f7a495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j + a_{m-j+1} \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" /> was false, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af9e724a0aa0979a915880b9173ee2d6dd421e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j + a_{m-j+1} \\ge n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a47e1cba42f55c36d8f5f5241b24e2519429b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le j \\le m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> Summing these inequalities together for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a47e1cba42f55c36d8f5f5241b24e2519429b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le j \\le m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/69465d0e2548fd07afcd349c2e21b58947419ba0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a_1+a_2+ \\dots a_m) \\ge m(n+1)\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich rearranges to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1fb85efc846bc414e5fa64d2b6deed425336c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1+a_2+ \\dots a_m}{m} \\ge \\frac{n+1}{2}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO\" title=\"1994 IMO\">1994 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144348\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 232/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7200/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.744      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.744      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Sa